# policy.matrix: what the gate of "harbor" decides, for every action and every kind of caller.
# Written by `pnpm policy:matrix` from the compiled policy (policy.yaml, identity.yaml) and the
# app's policy matrix (TestingHooks.policyMatrix); a test fails when it differs. Never edit it by
# hand: a difference here is a change in what the agent may do, to be reviewed as the policy is.
#
# Under each action (its level and its rules as the file writes them), a row per kind of caller.
# A row with one verdict holds for every call that caller can make; otherwise its lines split it
# by what the call carries, a|b meaning either value. "as <caller>" repeats that caller's verdicts.
#
# callers
#   anonymous               no one proven (level 0)
#   subject@1               member, level 1 (one of the app's subjects)
#   subject@2               member, level 2 (one of the app's subjects)
#   delegate:service_rep    broker, role service_rep, level 2
#   delegate:office_admin   broker, role office_admin, level 2
#   delegate:service_rep@1  broker, role service_rep, level 1 (a delegate below level 2)
#   unlisted-role           broker, role assistant, level 2 (a role the policy does not name)
#   roleless                broker with no role, level 2
#   other-party             visitor, level 2 (neither a subject nor of a delegate kind)
# what a call carries
#   purpose     none; entry-check, retry-check (the lifecycle's probes); a form's purpose
#   subject     own; inScope (a subject the delegates act for); outOfScope; unknown; empty
#   fields      exact; extra (one field more); missing (one field less: the subject's own when it is the only one)
#   confirmed   none; match (the caller confirmed exactly these values); mismatch
#   attempts    0; 3 (the maximum)
#   params      the policy matrix's named sets of values for the action
# verdicts: ALLOW; BLOCK <reason>; STEP_UP to <level>; NEEDS_HUMAN <reason>

purposes: report_claim needs level 2

verifyMember · level 0 · attempts(3)
  anonymous               attempts 0  ALLOW
                          attempts 3  NEEDS_HUMAN attempts
  subject@1               as anonymous
  subject@2               as anonymous
  delegate:service_rep    BLOCK not-subject
  delegate:office_admin   as delegate:service_rep
  delegate:service_rep@1  as delegate:service_rep
  unlisted-role           as delegate:service_rep
  roleless                as delegate:service_rep
  other-party             as delegate:service_rep

sendCode · level 1 · identity, scope(memberId)
  anonymous               purpose none|entry-check|retry-check  STEP_UP to 1
                          purpose report_claim                  STEP_UP to 2
  subject@1               purpose none|entry-check|retry-check, subject own, fields exact|extra           ALLOW
                          purpose none|entry-check|retry-check, subject own, fields missing               BLOCK scope
                          purpose none|entry-check|retry-check, subject inScope|outOfScope|unknown|empty  BLOCK scope
                          purpose report_claim                                                            STEP_UP to 2
  subject@2               subject own, fields exact|extra           ALLOW
                          subject own, fields missing               BLOCK scope
                          subject inScope|outOfScope|unknown|empty  BLOCK scope
  delegate:service_rep    BLOCK not-subject
  delegate:office_admin   as delegate:service_rep
  delegate:service_rep@1  as delegate:service_rep
  unlisted-role           as delegate:service_rep
  roleless                as delegate:service_rep
  other-party             as delegate:service_rep

